      "content": "Okay, it's getting more comprehensive, but I'm still a bit nervous about that compliance score. The marketing guys are being really difficult about the \"gate\" threshold.\n\nCan you try one more version where you really lean into the formal disclosure language? I need the count of those key terms to be much higher to ensure it clears the system on the first try. I know I said don't spam them, but if you can weave them into very formal, detailed-sounding legal caveats—like \"market risk factors,\" \"cautionary notes regarding risk,\" or \"warning against speculative risk\"—that should work. \n\nJust make sure the final text still actually looks like something a professional bank would publish, not just a list of words. Try to get that metric up significantly.",
